Actually that format is totally unsupported. BSD is the Base Security

model as provided by the Tru64 Security group.  Your configuration
should use some other letters than "BSD"... "SHAD" is fine, but then
make sure you keep the "BSD" there for compatibility.  There is a
siacfg utility that will help you create/manage the matrix.conf
file.  If you do things wrong and/or in an unsupported manner in
the matrix.conf - the 5.1b code will let you know that...



