In article <b3a8a5a8.0302180738.137de9b0@posting.google.com>,
stan jenereski <sjenereski@sysmaint.com> wrote:
>  A section is display in brackets as [fsize bsize cpq]

> so my question... does anyone know what the field cpq means?

It's cpg, cylinders per group. UFS divides the disk into cylinder groups,
and allocates space for related files and directory entries inthe same group.

This figure specifies how big those groups are.

