Giovanni Caramia wrote:

> I have modified /etc/inetd.conf writing
> 
> ssh2 stream tcp nowait root /usr/sbin/tcpd sshd2
> ...
> sshd2[12345]: FATAL ERROR: Creating listener failed: port 22 probably 
> already in use!

Sshd normally expects to run as a standalone daemon (you can still use
Tcp_Wrappers with it that way).  You'll either need to give it an option
to run it from inetd (-i) or take the line out of inetd.conf and run
sshd as a standalone daemon.

I hope that helps...

