Hi KG...

If there is nothing crucial on the system e.g. software, user
accounts, data etc... why not just go for a straight installation, and
wipe out what's already on the system?

At least then, you'll know its a "clean installation", and any
problems on the system will not be "historic", relating to previous
installations.

Just be sure you have access to the paper licenses before doing so, as
you'll be wiping the licenses off of the system with everything else,
and will need to re-register them.

All the best,

Tony A.
(UK)

