the _F64__F64_stat etc. part of the problem is fixed for the gcc 3.2.3, 3.3
and 3.4 releases:

	http://gcc.gnu.org/ml/gcc-patches/2003-02/msg01802.html

There are two variants of the gcc/config/alpha/osf.h patch, the latter one
is for the 3.2.x releases.  Also note that you need to install autogen to
regenerate fixincl.x after applying the patch.  Alternatively, you can get
the current gcc 3.2 branch from cvs.

I'm not entirely sure about the missing libiconv* symbols: this generally
happens when the bootstrap compiler finds and uses a copy of the GNU
libiconv <iconv.h> header, but later you link against the system libiconv.
If you really have GNU libiconv installed, you might try to use the
--with-libiconv-prefix=DIR configure switch to refer the gcc build to the
correct location.

	Rainer

