TyBreaker wrote:

> The extra tid-bit of info I picked up on Google was to include
> "pseudo-device alt" in the kernel config, recompile and reboot with the
> new kernel.  Now you'd think that info could have been included in the
> Tru64 section of the installation documentation that came with the card?

The other way to do it would have been...

Boot the generic kernel:

>>> boot -fi "genvmunix"

Build a new kernel:

# doconfig

Backup the old one:

# cp /vmunix /vmunix.sav

Copy the new one into place:

# cp /sys/$HOSTNAME/vmunix /vmunix

Halt the system:

# shutdown -h now

and boot:

>>> boot

Then you can configure the card.

-Brian


