Are you sure lpd is actually corrupt?  What are the symptoms?  If it is, 
it could be the result of a patch or updateinstall that is buggy (check 
for further patches if so).  I once had rdist break after a patch and 
simply rolled back the previous rdist binary which still worked fine.

Other things that may break it is an incorrect /etc/printcap.

You can also identify which installation subset lpd is in and extract is 
manually from the source CD to avoid any chance of a bad version.  Each 
subset in Tru64 4.x is simply a tar ball so you can uncompress it and 
then use tar to extract specific files.



