do you use standard ksh ?
do you setup site specific things in /etc/profile or /etc/csh.login ?

can you post ?
sysconfig -q proc
sysconfig -q generic
proc and generic records in /etc/sysconfigtab
/sys/conf/HOSTNAME

if nothing is defined in there, value is set in :

/sys/include/arch/alpha/vmparam.h :
# grep SSIZ /sys/include/arch/alpha/vmparam.h
#ifndef MAXSSIZ
#define MAXSSIZ         (1<<25)         /* max stack size */
#ifndef DFLSSIZ
#define DFLSSIZ         (1<<23)         /* initial stack size limit */

First of all, try to set 8192 as default( per_proc_stack_size =
8388608 ) in /etc/sysconfigtab proc subsystem.

This is the default, and I guess it can lead to trouble when you run
your processes under this value.

